   "name": "North Face",
   "grade": "4th AI2",
   "discipline": "ice",
   "overview": "Follows the prominent couloir up the middle of the peak. The first ascent stayed mostly on the rock walls, crossing between them to avoid snow and ice. After heavy winters snow persists in the couloir into fall and turns to blue alpine ice at about 50 degrees. The top-out squeezes via a natural bridge and lands near the summit. The way down depends on the approach. If returning to Cox Col or Lake Italy, take the south slopes (loose, class 2). If returning to Second Recess, take the Northwest ridge, also called the Glacier Route (class 2). The approach is one of the longest walk-ins for ice in the Sierra.",
