   "id": "ca_mount_mills_north_face",
   "area_id": "ca_mount_mills",
   "name": "North Face",
   "grade": "4th AI1",
   "discipline": "ice",
   "overview": "A trail to the trailhead via Ruby Lake is the way out: descend the East Couloir route, passing Mills Lake. The climb crosses the glacier to a clear couloir centered on the north face, ascends it (about 40 degrees) until a solid rock cap stops it, then veers right onto gentler terrain, mostly 3rd class, to reach the flat top before the summit itself.",
   "description": null,
   "approach": "Start at Mosquito Flat and hike the trail toward Mono Pass. From the pass go left (west) up an easy slope to the ridge top and scramble down the far side into the Fourth Recess, the trickiest part of the approach. Descend a broad, low-angle scree chute, turn south and go up the recess, passing Snow Lakes, to reach the glacier under the north face.",
   "descent_text": "The route ends on the summit plateau, crossed to the summit. The normal way off is the East Couloir route, passing Mills Lake to Ruby Lake where the trail back to the trailhead is picked up. Parties camped in the Fourth Recess can instead go back down the north face.",
